# Firebase CLI local state (deploy cache, emulator logs).
# Machine-specific and regenerated on every deploy — tracking it made the
# repo dirty after each `firebase deploy` and invited merge conflicts.
.firebase/
firebase-debug.log
firestore-debug.log

# Admin SDK private keys. The maintenance scripts under scripts/ need one, and
# backfill-audit-shape.cjs tells you to save it in the repo root — so this ignore
# has to exist BEFORE anyone follows that instruction. A committed key is a
# permanent grant of full read and write over every user's data, and revoking it
# means rotating it everywhere it is used; it is not a mistake that can be quietly
# undone by deleting the file in a later commit.
serviceAccountKey.json
*-firebase-adminsdk-*.json
**/serviceAccountKey.json

# Built output of the screen previews in preview/. Not shipped.
preview-dist/

# Compiled output of functions/. It was COMMITTED, all 102 files, until
# 2026-08-24 — and `functions/package.json` still points `main` at `lib/index.js`,
# so the instinct to keep it is understandable and wrong.
#
# Nothing needs it in git. `firebase.json` has a `predeploy` hook,
# `npm --prefix "$RESOURCE_DIR" run build`, so every functions deploy regenerates
# lib from source before packaging; a fresh clone with no lib/ deploys correctly.
# The functions test suite runs vitest straight off the TypeScript in src/. And the
# upload is NOT affected by this file: firebase-tools builds its archive from
# `functions.ignore` in firebase.json (defaulting to node_modules and .git) and
# never reads .gitignore — checked in
# lib/deploy/functions/prepareFunctionsUpload.js, not assumed, because getting it
# wrong would ship an empty function.
#
# What committing it cost: every run of the verification sweep regenerates 102
# .js/.js.map files, so the sweep itself dirtied the tree, and two branches
# touching one callable conflicted in generated output as well as in source.
functions/lib/
